# SRG-APP-000870-WSR-000270  -  CAT II
# The web server must, for password-based authentication, enforce
# organization-defined composition and complexity rules.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000870-WSR-000270
group:           V-264353
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-004066
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    Composition and complexity for native accounts, including those set
                 through Splunk Web, are entirely configurable in authentication.conf
                 [splunk_auth]: minPasswordUppercase, minPasswordLowercase,
                 minPasswordDigit, minPasswordSpecial, and minPasswordLength are enforced
                 at password set and modify time, and expirePasswordDays bounds the
                 password's life. The composition rules are organization-defined, and the
                 values asserted below are the ones the benchmark authority sets for this
                 product in SPLK-CL-000340 through SPLK-CL-000400.

governs:         authentication.conf - How users sign in, and the password rules applied to local accounts.

check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordUppercase min 1
check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordLowercase min 1
check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordDigit min 1
check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordSpecial min 1
check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordLength min 15
check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] expirePasswordDays max 60
check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] expirePasswordDays min 1
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] expirePasswordDays https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordDigit https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordLength https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-cloud-platform/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.2.2510/manage-credentials-and-keys/configure-a-splunk-enterprise-password-policy-using-the-authentication.conf-configuration-file
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordLowercase https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordSpecial https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordUppercase https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The composition and complexity rules themselves - organization-defined;
                 the values asserted here are those the product STIG sets for this product,
                 and an organization imposing stricter rules still passes because each
                 condition is a minimum or a maximum.
external:        Where authType is LDAP, SAML, or ProxySSO, [splunk_auth] governs native
                 accounts only and complexity for everyone else is enforced by the
                 directory service or identity provider.
external:        expirePasswordDays takes effect only when expireUserAccounts is enabled
                 per the spec; that setting is not among this requirement's determined
                 check rows, so the condition is limited to the value SPLK-CL-000400 names
                 and the expiration switch should be confirmed alongside it.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/authentication.conf.spec:437 ([splunk_auth]), :441
                 (minPasswordLength, default 8), :450 (minPasswordUppercase, default 0),
                 :459 (minPasswordLowercase, default 0), :468 (minPasswordDigit, default
                 0), :477 (minPasswordSpecial, default 0), :487 (expirePasswordDays,
                 0-3650, default 90), :505 (expireUserAccounts, default false);
                 SPLK-CL-000340, 000350, 000360, 000370, 000380, 000400 check and fix text
finding:         The application does not enforce the required password composition and
                 complexity rules for native accounts - one or more of authentication.conf
                 [splunk_auth] minPasswordUppercase, minPasswordLowercase,
                 minPasswordDigit, minPasswordSpecial (each must be at least 1),
                 minPasswordLength (at least 15), or expirePasswordDays (no more than 60)
                 is missing or weaker than the product STIG requires; this determination is
                 from the perspective of the application layer alone, and governs native
                 accounts only where authentication is delegated to a directory service or
                 identity provider.
